{"account":{"geo":"maghreb","title":"The Maghreb, 1100 BCE to now","author":"Claude (Opus 5.5) for Jeremy Parra","extent":{"lon":[-17,12],"lat":[27,38]},"t_from":-1100,"t_to":2025,"cite":1,"note":"The second account. It shares Punic, Latin, Arabic, Tamazight, Islam and Judaism with Iberia's — the first test of reconciling two tellings."},"colonies":[{"tribe":"berber","keyframes":[[-1100,-6.0,32.5,450],[700,-6.0,32.5,450],[1200,-6.0,32.5,420,0.95],[1600,-6.0,32.5,380,0.9],[1900,-6.0,32.5,350,0.8],[2025,-6.0,32.5,330,0.7]],"note":"The tongue of the Maghreb before Carthage, and still a mother tongue for a large minority — it held the mountains (Rif, Atlas, Kabylie, Aurès) while Arabic took the cities and plains."},{"tribe":"berber","keyframes":[[-1100,5.2,36.0,300],[1050,5.2,36.0,280],[1500,5.2,36.0,180],[1900,5.2,36.0,120],[2025,5.2,36.0,110]],"label":"Kabylie & the Aurès"},{"tribe":"berber","keyframes":[[-1100,9.5,34.8,250],[0,9.5,34.8,220,0.8],[700,9.5,34.8,220],[1050,9.5,34.8,180],[1300,9.5,34.8,60],[1600,9.5,34.8,30],[2025,9.5,34.8,25]],"label":"Ifriqiya"},{"tribe":"berber","keyframes":[[-1100,5.5,25.5,450],[2025,5.5,25.5,450,0.8]],"label":"the Tuareg Sahara"},{"tribe":"berber","keyframes":[[-1100,3.67,32.49,60],[2025,3.67,32.49,60]],"label":"the Mzab"},{"tribe":"berber","keyframes":[[-1100,12.0,31.9,100],[2025,12.0,31.9,60]],"label":"Jabal Nafusa"},{"tribe":"punic","keyframes":[[-814,10.32,36.85,0],[-800,10.32,36.85,60],[-500,10.32,36.85,180],[-300,10.32,36.85,250],[-146,10.32,36.85,250],[0,10.32,36.85,160,0.7],[200,10.32,36.85,100,0.5],[400,10.32,36.85,50,0.4],[450,10.32,36.85,0]],"note":"Carthage's tongue outlived Carthage by six centuries: Augustine, around 400, still met Punic-speaking peasants."},{"tribe":"punic","keyframes":[[-500,7.77,36.9,0],[-400,7.77,36.9,60],[-146,7.77,36.9,80],[300,7.77,36.9,60],[450,7.77,36.9,0]],"label":"Hippo"},{"tribe":"punic","keyframes":[[-600,14.29,32.64,0],[-500,14.29,32.64,60],[200,14.29,32.64,60],[400,14.29,32.64,0]],"label":"Leptis"},{"tribe":"punic","keyframes":[[-700,-6.12,35.2,0],[-600,-6.12,35.2,40],[-100,-6.12,35.2,40],[50,-6.12,35.2,0]],"label":"Lixus"},{"tribe":"latin","keyframes":[[-146,9.6,36.2,0],[-100,9.6,36.2,120],[100,9.6,36.2,280],[430,9.6,36.2,280],[534,9.6,36.2,220,0.8],[700,9.6,36.2,150,0.6],[750,9.6,36.2,0]],"note":"Roman Africa was among the most Latin provinces of the empire — Apuleius, Tertullian, Augustine wrote here."},{"tribe":"latin","keyframes":[[-46,6.5,36.2,0],[50,6.5,36.2,200],[430,6.5,36.2,200],[700,6.5,36.2,100],[750,6.5,36.2,0]],"label":"Numidia"},{"tribe":"latin","keyframes":[[40,2.2,36.3,0],[100,2.2,36.3,150],[430,2.2,36.3,120],[550,2.2,36.3,0]],"label":"Mauretania Caesariensis"},{"tribe":"latin","keyframes":[[40,-5.6,35.0,0],[100,-5.6,35.0,110],[430,-5.6,35.0,60],[500,-5.6,35.0,0]],"label":"Tingitana"},{"tribe":"african_romance","keyframes":[[650,9.8,36.0,0],[750,9.8,36.0,200],[900,9.8,36.0,160,0.7],[1050,9.8,36.0,100,0.5],[1150,9.8,36.0,40,0.4],[1200,9.8,36.0,0]],"note":"What Latin became in Africa. Still spoken in Ifriqiya's towns into the 1100s — al-Idrisi heard it at Gafsa in 1154 — then gone without a written trace of its own."},{"tribe":"african_romance","keyframes":[[700,8.78,34.42,0],[800,8.78,34.42,60],[1154,8.78,34.42,50],[1200,8.78,34.42,0]],"label":"Gafsa"},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[670,10.1,35.68,0],[700,10.1,35.68,80],[900,10.1,35.68,200],[1050,10.1,35.68,250],[1100,10.1,35.68,330],[1500,10.1,35.68,380],[2025,10.1,35.68,400]],"note":"Arrived with the armies that founded Kairouan in 670 but stayed a language of cities and courts until the Banu Hilal migrations of the 1050s carried Bedouin Arabic across the steppe."},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[789,-5.0,34.0,0],[820,-5.0,34.0,80],[1200,-5.0,34.0,160],[1600,-5.0,34.0,280],[1900,-5.0,34.0,330],[2025,-5.0,34.0,380]],"label":"Fez and the Moroccan cities"},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[750,2.5,35.5,0],[900,2.5,35.5,120],[1100,2.5,35.5,260],[1500,2.5,35.5,350],[2025,2.5,35.5,380]],"label":"the Algerian plains"},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[1050,1.0,33.5,0],[1150,1.0,33.5,300],[1400,1.0,33.5,450],[2025,1.0,33.5,450]],"label":"the Hilalian steppe"},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[1400,-12.0,23.0,0],[1600,-12.0,23.0,400],[2025,-12.0,23.0,450]],"label":"Hassaniya, the western Sahara"},{"tribe":"judeo_arabic","keyframes":[[800,-5.0,34.03,0],[900,-5.0,34.03,30],[1950,-5.0,34.03,30],[1970,-5.0,34.03,5],[1980,-5.0,34.03,0]],"note":"Arabic in Hebrew letters — the language of Maimonides' letters and of Fez's mellah."},{"tribe":"judeo_arabic","keyframes":[[700,10.86,33.81,0],[750,10.86,33.81,20],[2025,10.86,33.81,10]],"label":"Djerba"},{"tribe":"judeo_arabic","keyframes":[[900,3.06,36.75,0],[950,3.06,36.75,20],[1962,3.06,36.75,20],[1963,3.06,36.75,0]],"label":"Algiers"},{"tribe":"judeo_arabic","keyframes":[[900,6.61,36.36,0],[950,6.61,36.36,20],[1962,6.61,36.36,20],[1963,6.61,36.36,0]],"label":"Constantine"},{"tribe":"judeo_arabic","keyframes":[[1100,-7.99,31.63,0],[1150,-7.99,31.63,20],[1960,-7.99,31.63,20],[1975,-7.99,31.63,0]],"label":"Marrakesh"},{"tribe":"judeo_arabic","keyframes":[[900,10.18,36.8,0],[950,10.18,36.8,25],[1956,10.18,36.8,25],[1967,10.18,36.8,8],[2025,10.18,36.8,4]],"label":"Tunis"},{"tribe":"ladino","keyframes":[[1492,-5.6,35.65,0],[1500,-5.6,35.65,55],[1950,-5.6,35.65,55],[1975,-5.6,35.65,0]],"note":"Haketia: the Judeo-Spanish of Tetouan and Tangier."},{"tribe":"french","keyframes":[[1830,3.0,36.3,0],[1850,3.0,36.3,150],[1900,3.0,36.3,300],[1962,3.0,36.3,380],[1970,3.0,36.3,300,0.7],[2025,3.0,36.3,350,0.6]],"note":"Brought by conquest in 1830; outlasted the empire as a language of schooling, business and emigration."},{"tribe":"french","keyframes":[[1881,10.1,36.5,0],[1920,10.1,36.5,150],[1956,10.1,36.5,200],[2025,10.1,36.5,180,0.6]],"label":"Tunisia"},{"tribe":"french","keyframes":[[1912,-6.5,33.8,0],[1940,-6.5,33.8,200],[1956,-6.5,33.8,220],[2025,-6.5,33.8,250,0.6]],"label":"Morocco"},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[1912,-5.3,35.2,0],[1930,-5.3,35.2,100,0.6],[1956,-5.3,35.2,100,0.5],[2025,-5.3,35.2,60,0.4]],"label":"the northern protectorate"},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[1509,-0.64,35.7,0],[1520,-0.64,35.7,30],[1792,-0.64,35.7,30],[1800,-0.64,35.7,0]],"label":"Oran presidio"},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[1850,-0.64,35.7,0],[1900,-0.64,35.7,80,0.7],[1962,-0.64,35.7,80,0.7],[1963,-0.64,35.7,0]],"label":"Spanish settlers in Oran"},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[1640,-5.32,35.89,0],[1668,-5.32,35.89,15],[2025,-5.32,35.89,15]],"label":"Ceuta"},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[1497,-2.94,35.29,0],[1500,-2.94,35.29,12],[2025,-2.94,35.29,12]],"label":"Melilla"},{"tribe":"native","keyframes":[[-1100,-6.0,32.5,500],[300,-6.0,32.5,450,0.8],[700,-6.0,32.5,300,0.6],[900,-6.0,32.5,0]],"note":"Libyan-Berber cults of springs, mountains, ancestors and kings."},{"tribe":"native","keyframes":[[-1100,6.0,35.0,400],[0,6.0,35.0,300,0.6],[400,6.0,35.0,150,0.3],[700,6.0,35.0,0]]},{"tribe":"native","keyframes":[[-1100,5.5,25.5,450],[700,5.5,25.5,400,0.6],[1100,5.5,25.5,100,0.3],[1300,5.5,25.5,0]],"label":"the Sahara"},{"tribe":"phoenician","keyframes":[[-814,10.32,36.85,0],[-800,10.32,36.85,50],[-500,10.32,36.85,200],[-146,10.32,36.85,250],[-100,10.32,36.85,150,0.7],[200,10.32,36.85,100,0.5],[350,10.32,36.85,0]],"note":"Baal Hammon and Tanit at Carthage; under Rome, Baal Hammon lived on as 'African Saturn'."},{"tribe":"phoenician","keyframes":[[-600,14.29,32.64,0],[-500,14.29,32.64,60],[100,14.29,32.64,40],[200,14.29,32.64,0]],"label":"Leptis"},{"tribe":"roman","keyframes":[[-146,9.5,36.0,0],[-50,9.5,36.0,150],[100,9.5,36.0,330],[250,9.5,36.0,350],[380,9.5,36.0,150,0.5],[420,9.5,36.0,0]]},{"tribe":"roman","keyframes":[[40,-1.0,35.3,0],[100,-1.0,35.3,250,0.7],[300,-1.0,35.3,200,0.6],[400,-1.0,35.3,0]],"label":"Mauretania"},{"tribe":"catholic","keyframes":[[180,8.5,36.0,0],[250,8.5,36.0,200,0.7],[400,8.5,36.0,350,0.9],[430,8.5,36.0,350],[534,8.5,36.0,330],[698,8.5,36.0,250,0.7],[800,8.5,36.0,150,0.4],[1000,8.5,36.0,80,0.3],[1100,8.5,36.0,30,0.2],[1159,8.5,36.0,0]],"note":"Africa was Latin Christianity's first heartland — Tertullian, Cyprian, Augustine — and its communities lasted five centuries under Islam, ending only with the Almohads."},{"tribe":"catholic","keyframes":[[250,-1.0,35.3,0],[400,-1.0,35.3,150,0.6],[700,-1.0,35.3,80,0.3],[800,-1.0,35.3,0]],"label":"Mauretania"},{"tribe":"catholic","keyframes":[[1830,3.0,36.3,0],[1870,3.0,36.3,150,0.5],[1954,3.0,36.3,200,0.6],[1962,3.0,36.3,50,0.2],[1970,3.0,36.3,0]],"label":"the settlers of French Algeria"},{"tribe":"catholic","keyframes":[[1881,10.1,36.7,0],[1930,10.1,36.7,100,0.4],[1956,10.1,36.7,60,0.3],[1965,10.1,36.7,0]],"label":"Tunisia's Europeans"},{"tribe":"catholic","keyframes":[[1912,-7.6,33.6,0],[1950,-7.6,33.6,100,0.4],[1956,-7.6,33.6,60,0.3],[1970,-7.6,33.6,0]],"label":"Morocco's Europeans"},{"tribe":"donatist","keyframes":[[311,6.5,35.8,0],[330,6.5,35.8,250,0.8],[411,6.5,35.8,280,0.8],[430,6.5,35.8,200,0.6],[600,6.5,35.8,60,0.3],[700,6.5,35.8,0]],"note":"Numidia's own church, condemned at Carthage in 411 — a creed that tracked the Berber countryside against the Latin cities."},{"tribe":"arian","keyframes":[[429,9.8,36.4,0],[439,9.8,36.4,180,0.5],[534,9.8,36.4,180,0.5],[540,9.8,36.4,0]],"note":"The Vandals' creed, imposed on a Catholic province."},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[100,10.1,36.0,0],[200,10.1,36.0,50],[1000,10.1,36.0,60],[1950,10.1,36.0,60],[1967,10.1,36.0,20],[2025,10.1,36.0,10]],"note":"Older here than Islam: Jews in Carthage by the 2nd century; Kairouan's scholars; the Sephardim of 1492. Nearly all left for Israel and France between 1948 and 1970. Djerba's El Ghriba synagogue remains."},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[200,-5.5,33.5,0],[800,-5.5,33.5,80],[1492,-5.5,33.5,120],[1948,-5.5,33.5,150],[1967,-5.5,33.5,60],[2025,-5.5,33.5,10]],"label":"Morocco"},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[300,3.0,36.4,0],[900,3.0,36.4,60],[1870,3.0,36.4,80],[1962,3.0,36.4,80],[1963,3.0,36.4,0]],"label":"Algeria"},{"tribe":"islam","keyframes":[[670,10.0,35.5,0],[700,10.0,35.5,150,0.5],[800,10.0,35.5,250],[1000,10.0,35.5,330],[2025,10.0,35.5,330]],"note":"Conversion was slow and political: Berbers took Islam on their own terms — first as Kharijites against the caliphs, then as Almoravid and Almohad reformers. Maliki Sunnism won by the 1000s."},{"tribe":"islam","keyframes":[[700,2.5,35.3,0],[750,2.5,35.3,150,0.4],[1000,2.5,35.3,300,0.9],[1100,2.5,35.3,350],[2025,2.5,35.3,380]]},{"tribe":"islam","keyframes":[[700,-6.0,32.5,0],[740,-6.0,32.5,200,0.4],[900,-6.0,32.5,350,0.8],[1100,-6.0,32.5,450],[2025,-6.0,32.5,450]]},{"tribe":"islam","keyframes":[[900,-1.0,26.0,0],[1100,-1.0,26.0,400,0.7],[1400,-1.0,26.0,500],[2025,-1.0,26.0,500]],"label":"the Sahara"},{"tribe":"kharijite","keyframes":[[740,1.33,35.37,0],[777,1.33,35.37,150],[909,1.33,35.37,150],[920,1.33,35.37,40],[950,1.33,35.37,0]],"note":"The creed of the Berber revolt of 740: any righteous believer may lead, 'even an Ethiopian slave'. It ruled from Tahert and Sijilmasa; its Ibadi branch survives in the Mzab, on Djerba and in the Nafusa hills."},{"tribe":"kharijite","keyframes":[[757,-4.27,31.28,0],[770,-4.27,31.28,100,0.8],[976,-4.27,31.28,80],[1000,-4.27,31.28,0]],"label":"Sijilmasa (Sufri)"},{"tribe":"kharijite","keyframes":[[750,12.0,31.9,0],[800,12.0,31.9,100],[2025,12.0,31.9,60]],"label":"Jabal Nafusa"},{"tribe":"kharijite","keyframes":[[1000,3.67,32.49,0],[1050,3.67,32.49,60],[2025,3.67,32.49,60]],"label":"the Mzab"},{"tribe":"kharijite","keyframes":[[800,10.86,33.81,0],[900,10.86,33.81,40],[2025,10.86,33.81,30]],"label":"Djerba"},{"tribe":"ismaili","keyframes":[[893,9.0,35.6,0],[909,9.0,35.6,150,0.5],[950,9.0,35.6,200,0.5],[973,9.0,35.6,150,0.4],[1048,9.0,35.6,0]],"note":"Preached among the Kutama Berbers of Kabylie; the Fatimids rode it to a caliphate, then left for Cairo. Their Zirid successors broke with it in 1048."},{"tribe":"secular","keyframes":[[1956,10.18,36.8,0],[2025,10.18,36.8,80,0.4]],"note":"Bourguiba's state secularism, 1956 on.","label":"Tunis"},{"tribe":"farming","keyframes":[[-300,8.8,36.2,150],[-146,8.8,36.2,200],[100,8.8,36.2,330],[700,8.8,36.2,250,0.7],[1100,8.8,36.2,200,0.6],[1900,8.8,36.2,300,0.8],[2025,8.8,36.2,300,0.8]],"note":"Africa was Rome's granary. After the 1050s much of the plain went over to herds; colonial Algeria planted it with vines for French wine."},{"tribe":"farming","keyframes":[[-1100,-6.5,33.5,200,0.5],[1100,-6.5,33.5,250,0.7],[1930,-6.5,33.5,350],[2025,-6.5,33.5,350]],"label":"the Moroccan plains"},{"tribe":"herding","keyframes":[[-1100,2.0,33.5,400,0.7],[1100,2.0,33.5,500],[1900,2.0,33.5,450,0.8],[2025,2.0,33.5,350,0.5]],"note":"The high steppe between Atlas and Sahara: sheep and camels on the move."},{"tribe":"herding","keyframes":[[-1100,-6.0,32.0,300],[2025,-6.0,32.0,250,0.5]],"label":"Atlas transhumance"},{"tribe":"irrigation","keyframes":[[700,-4.27,31.28,0],[800,-4.27,31.28,60],[2025,-4.27,31.28,60]],"note":"Oasis farming on foggaras and khettaras — tunnels that lead groundwater to the palms.","label":"Tafilalt"},{"tribe":"irrigation","keyframes":[[900,-0.29,27.87,0],[1000,-0.29,27.87,120],[2025,-0.29,27.87,100]],"label":"Touat"},{"tribe":"irrigation","keyframes":[[1050,3.67,32.49,0],[1100,3.67,32.49,40],[2025,3.67,32.49,40]],"label":"the Mzab"},{"tribe":"irrigation","keyframes":[[-500,8.1,33.9,60],[2025,8.1,33.9,60]],"label":"the Jerid"},{"tribe":"irrigation","keyframes":[[-500,-6.0,30.3,60],[2025,-6.0,30.3,60]],"label":"the Draa"},{"tribe":"irrigation","keyframes":[[1070,-8.0,31.6,0],[1100,-8.0,31.6,80],[2025,-8.0,31.6,80]],"label":"the Haouz of Marrakesh"},{"tribe":"caravan","keyframes":[[750,-4.27,31.28,0],[800,-4.27,31.28,100],[1400,-4.27,31.28,120],[1600,-4.27,31.28,80],[1800,-4.27,31.28,30],[1900,-4.27,31.28,0]],"note":"Salt went south, gold and slaves came north. The Maghreb's cities were ports on the shore of the Sahara as much as of the Mediterranean.","label":"Sijilmasa"},{"tribe":"caravan","keyframes":[[800,5.33,31.95,0],[900,5.33,31.95,80],[1500,5.33,31.95,80],[1900,5.33,31.95,0]],"label":"Ouargla"},{"tribe":"caravan","keyframes":[[300,9.5,30.13,0],[400,9.5,30.13,60],[1800,9.5,30.13,80],[1900,9.5,30.13,20],[1930,9.5,30.13,0]],"label":"Ghadames"},{"tribe":"caravan","keyframes":[[1000,-0.29,27.87,0],[1100,-0.29,27.87,90],[1800,-0.29,27.87,90],[1900,-0.29,27.87,0]],"label":"Touat"},{"tribe":"caravan","keyframes":[[1000,-4.97,23.6,0],[1100,-4.97,23.6,60],[1585,-4.97,23.6,60],[1600,-4.97,23.6,0]],"label":"Taghaza salt"},{"tribe":"caravan","keyframes":[[1100,-1.32,34.88,0],[1300,-1.32,34.88,60],[1550,-1.32,34.88,60],[1600,-1.32,34.88,0]],"label":"Tlemcen"},{"tribe":"caravan","keyframes":[[1070,-7.99,31.63,0],[1100,-7.99,31.63,60],[1600,-7.99,31.63,80],[1800,-7.99,31.63,30],[1900,-7.99,31.63,0]],"label":"Marrakesh"},{"tribe":"seafaring","keyframes":[[-800,10.32,36.85,0],[-700,10.32,36.85,80],[-146,10.32,36.85,100],[-100,10.32,36.85,30],[100,10.32,36.85,50,0.6],[700,10.32,36.85,20],[900,10.32,36.85,0]],"note":"Carthage was a sea power before it was anything else.","label":"Carthage's harbours"},{"tribe":"seafaring","keyframes":[[900,10.2,36.6,40],[2025,10.2,36.6,50]],"label":"Tunisian fisheries"},{"tribe":"seafaring","keyframes":[[1760,-9.7,31.0,0],[1800,-9.7,31.0,40],[2025,-9.7,31.0,70]],"label":"the Atlantic coast"},{"tribe":"corsairs","keyframes":[[1516,3.06,36.75,0],[1530,3.06,36.75,100],[1650,3.06,36.75,150],[1750,3.06,36.75,80],[1816,3.06,36.75,40],[1830,3.06,36.75,0]],"note":"From the 1500s to 1830 privateering was a state industry here — ships seized, Christians ransomed or enslaved — the mirror of Malta's knights doing the same to Muslims.","label":"Algiers"},{"tribe":"corsairs","keyframes":[[1550,10.18,36.8,0],[1600,10.18,36.8,80],[1700,10.18,36.8,60],[1816,10.18,36.8,20],[1830,10.18,36.8,0]],"label":"Tunis"},{"tribe":"corsairs","keyframes":[[1610,-6.8,34.04,0],[1627,-6.8,34.04,70],[1700,-6.8,34.04,40],[1800,-6.8,34.04,10],[1830,-6.8,34.04,0]],"label":"S